Duplicate logic: the SIGTERM and SIGINT handlers are identical. Extracting a shared handler would reduce maintenance cost and the risk of them drifting apart if the error-reporting logic ever changes. Consider:

```ts
function onTerminate() { void stop().catch((e) => { console.error(JSON.stringify({ error: String(e) })); process.exit(1); }); }
process.on("SIGTERM", onTerminate);
process.on("SIGINT", onTerminate);
```

Note `stop()`, `rt`, and `root` are all in scope, so lifting to a named function is safe.

