The default tick interval `15000` (15s) — a business number — is hardcoded twice. If the default ever changes, both sites must be updated in lockstep, risking drift (one copy could be missed, silently altering startup behavior). The checklist flags business-related hardcoded numbers as prohibited. Extract a named constant so there is a single source of truth:

```ts
const DEFAULT_TICK_MS = 15000;
const rawTickMs = Number(process.env.UPPER_TICK_MS ?? DEFAULT_TICK_MS);
const tickMs = Number.isFinite(rawTickMs) && rawTickMs > 0 ? rawTickMs : DEFAULT_TICK_MS;
```

This also mirrors the `parseTickMs(raw, fallback = 15000)` pattern already used in runtime.ts, keeping the two consistent.

